================================================================================
1. PROJECT PURPOSE & OFFICIAL DISTRIBUTION
================================================================================

Windows AD Remote Administration Control Center Enterprise ("WADRACC", formerly
known as "ADRC", or "the Software"), developed by Askarali Mattummal
("Author"), is a Windows-based administration application originally created for
personal use to simplify everyday Active Directory and enterprise Windows
infrastructure management.

Following requests from colleagues and fellow IT professionals, WADRACC has been
made publicly available as freeware to assist system administrators, network
engineers, domain administrators, and helpdesk specialists.

The Software is specifically designed to provide:
  * Safe, non-intrusive administrative operations.
  * Fully portable execution — requiring no installer, agents, or external
    third-party DLL dependencies.
  * Lightweight, responsive, and resource-efficient operation.
  * Centralized Active Directory user, group, and computer management.
  * Workstation remote administration, including Remote Shadow and RDP.
  * Printer queue, mapped drive, software inventory, and share management.
  * Live system telemetry, 24/7 network monitoring, and diagnostic suites.
  * Active Directory security assessment and server health auditing tools.

The Software (including its main executable, companion executables such as
ADRC_IdleAgent, ADRC_MonitorCoordinator, and ADRC_DiskScanner, administrative
scripts, and documentation) is distributed free of charge under the terms of
this proprietary license.

